s_expandable': True, 'note_tweet_results': {'result': {'id': 'Tm90ZVR3ZWV0OjE4ODUwNDg2NzI2NjE5NTQ1NjA=', 'text': 'I did a quick search to find anything that points to Maggie having any scientific training or any training that would qualify her to speak about "science."\n\nNothing.\n\nMaggie Hassan attended Brown University, where she earned a B.A. in history in 1980. Hassan then went on to obtain a J.D. from Northeastern University School of Law in 1985. So, no formal training in science or the philosophy of science.\n\nWork History\n\n- Worked at the Boston law firm Palmer & Dodge from 1985 to 1992\n- Served as associate general counsel for Brigham and Women\'s Hospital from 1993 to 1996\n- Worked as an attorney at Sullivan, Weinstein & McQuay, a Boston corporate defense and business law firm, starting in 1996\n\nPolitical Career\n\nHassan\'s political career began in 1999 when she was appointed as a citizen advisor to the New Hampshire Advisory Committee to the Adequacy in Education and Finance Commission[9]. Her subsequent political roles include:\n\n- New Hampshire State Senator (2004-2010)\n- Governor of New Hampshire (2013-2017)\n- U.S. Senator for New Hampshire (2017-present)\n\nRecent News and Actions\n\n1. In November 2024, Hassan held her 7th Annual Innovate New Hampshire Forum to support the state\'s entrepreneurs.\n2. In January 2025, Hassan voted to advance Rep. Collins\' nomination as Secretary of Veterans Affairs.\n3. Hassan recently shared her personal story about suffering a miscarriage and needing reproductive care, discussing its relevance to the 2024 presidential election.\n4. In May 2024, Hassan was named the most bipartisan member of Congress by the nonpartisan Common Ground Committee.\n\n Questionable Actions\n\n1. Hassan\'s husband, Tom Hassan, was involved in mishandling a sexual abuse scandal at Phillips Exeter Academy while serving as principal. An independent investigation found that the school\'s leadership, including Tom Hassan, failed to properly handle allegations of misconduct\n\n2. In 2012, Hassan\'s gubernatorial campaign appointed a former teacher who had admitted to sexual misconduct to leadership committees, despite his forced retirement from Phillips Exeter Academy in 2011. Hassan later apologized for this oversight[\n\n3. Hassan has faced criticism from both Republicans and Democrats for her stance on immigration and border security. Her visit to the U.S.-Mexico border in April 2022 was seen by some as a political ploy and led to backlash from Latino leaders within her own party', 'entity_set': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'urls': [], 'user_mentions': []}, 'richtext': {'richtext_tags': []}, 'media': {'inline_media': []}}}}, 'legacy': {'bookmark_count': 0, 'bookmarked': False, 'created_at': 'Thu Jan 30 19:33:20 +0000 2025', 'conversation_id_str': '1885020473618055460', 'display_text_range': [14, 288], 'entities': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'timestamps': [], 'urls': [], 'user_mentions': [{'id_str': '69156861', 'name': 'Chief Nerd', 'screen_name': 'TheChiefNerd', 'indices': [0, 13]}]}, 'favorite_count': 3, 'favorited': False, 'full_text': '@TheChiefNerd I did a quick search to find anything that points to Maggie having any scientific training or any training that would qualify her to speak about "science."\n\nNothing.\n\nMaggie Hassan attended Brown University, where she earned a B.A. in history in 1980. Hassan then went on to', 'in_reply_to_screen_name': 'TheChiefNerd', 'in_reply_to_status_id_str': '1885020473618055460', 'in_reply_to_user_id_str': '69156861', 'is_quote_status': False, 'lang': 'en', 'quote_count': 0, 'reply_count': 1, 'retweet_count': 1, 'retweeted': False, 'user_id_str': '1663619963058540544', 'id_str': '1885048672892703205'}}, '_legacy': {'bookmark_count': 0, 'bookmarked': False, 'created_at': 'Thu Jan 30 19:33:20 +0000 2025', 'conversation_id_str': '1885020473618055460', 'display_text_range': [14, 288], 'entities': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'timestamps': []